{
  "step_1": "The decision reason focuses on whether a lottery has a sure outcome (i.e., an outcome with 100% probability). In the decision problem, Lottery A has two outcomes (1000 Euros with 50% and 0 Euros with 50%), so it does not have a sure outcome. Lottery B offers 500 Euros with 100% probability, so it does have a sure outcome. Therefore, the decision reason can be applied: it would prefer Lottery A (without a sure outcome) over Lottery B (with a sure outcome).",
